# Each mutation swaps a piece of Queue.tla for a plausible bug in the code it models and names
# the rule that must break on it. `scripts/formal --mutations` must print DETECTED for each.

# Before 2026-11-06: a process starting on a Library requeued every running job, even one
# another live process (the app, `argus work`) was running.
mutation requeue_stale_jobs requeues every running job, whoever runs it
detects NoDoubleRun on p2 RunnerSeesRunning on p2
- Stale(p, j) == status[j] = "running" /\ (owner[j] = p \/ ~up[owner[j]])
+ Stale(p, j) == status[j] = "running"

# Before 2026-11-06: enqueue_job read for a job with the same dedupe key, then inserted.
mutation enqueue checks the dedupe key and inserts in two statements
detects OneActivePerKey on p1
-        ELSE status' = [status EXCEPT ![j] = "queued"] /\ UNCHANGED ins
+        ELSE ins' = [ins EXCEPT ![c] = j] /\ UNCHANGED status

mutation the periodic requeue takes jobs a live process is running
detects RunnerSeesRunning on p1
-     /\ up[p] /\ \E j \in Jobs : status[j] = "running" /\ ~up[owner[j]]
-     /\ status' = [j \in Jobs |-> IF status[j] = "running" /\ ~up[owner[j]] THEN "queued" ELSE status[j]]
+     /\ up[p] /\ \E j \in Jobs : status[j] = "running"
+     /\ status' = [j \in Jobs |-> IF status[j] = "running" THEN "queued" ELSE status[j]]

mutation claim takes a job without checking it is still queued
detects NoDoubleRun on p2
-     /\ up[p] /\ work[p] = 0 /\ status[j] = "queued"
+     /\ up[p] /\ work[p] = 0 /\ status[j] \in Active

mutation settle writes its outcome over a cancel
detects CancelSticks on p1
-     /\ status' = [status EXCEPT ![work[p]] = IF @ = "running" THEN to ELSE @]
+     /\ status' = [status EXCEPT ![work[p]] = to]

mutation retry queues a failed job whose key already has one queued
detects OneActivePerKey on p1
-                        /\ ~\E k \in Jobs : Key[k] = Key[j] /\ status[k] \in Active
+                        /\ TRUE
